  "decision": {
    "minimum_relative_reduction": 0.3,
    "minimum_baseline_correction_events": 3,
    "correction_event_definition": "For one anonymous arm and case, true only when the blind adjudicator records a non-empty post-implementation instruction requiring a code change to satisfy the frozen request, persona contract, DoD, or verification command; approvals, pre-execution questions, and adoption decisions are excluded.",
    "correction_rate_denominator": "ten_paired_cases_per_arm",
    "correction_evidence_binding": "Each signed blind-adjudication v4 case entry retains the registered arm-mapping SHA-256 outside the evaluator-visible packet and binds anonymous arm_a and arm_b quality decisions to that packet. Each signed execution receipt supplies final diff and verification descriptors whose referenced artifact has the exact canonical fields schema_version, artifact_kind, content, and content_sha256; explicit arm, executor, skill, and workflow metadata is rejected as artifact fields, and each forbidden identifier token is rejected case-insensitively anywhere in content regardless of wrapper. The packet builder accepts no caller-selected evaluation artifact, extracts both descriptors from the validated terminal bundle using root-qualified source identity, creates neutral no-replace canonical copies, and includes the frozen request, persona contract with its observable persona-fidelity rubric, DoD, and verification command text plus their hashes. Every adjudicated arm records a non-empty evidence statement and pass boolean for each frozen persona-fidelity criterion; persona_fidelity_pass must equal the conjunction of those criterion results. persona-decision reopens every packet and nested artifact with O_NOFOLLOW, rejects study-wide artifact reuse, and compares the evaluation contract with the terminal dry-run and enrollment chain before revealing direct_codex and omc_persona.",
